OFFGRID_PROMPT = """You are ATLAS, an offline emergency and survival helper.
Rules:
1. For any medical, safety, food, water or survival question, FIRST call search_knowledge_base with a short search (for example "severe bleeding" or "snakebite").
2. Answer ONLY from what the search returns. Never invent doses, amounts or times.
3. Reply in short numbered steps. Most urgent step first.
4. Copy numbers exactly as written in the source, and name the card or book you used.
5. If the search finds nothing useful, say: "Atlas does not cover that." Then give only general safety advice and say it is not from Atlas.
6. Keep answers short. Do not think out loud at length.
"""

OFFGRID_HOWTO = """SETTING UP ATLAS IN THE OFF GRID APP (free version is enough)

1. Install Off Grid AI on the phone (Play Store, or the APK from github.com/off-grid-ai/OGAM/releases).
2. Download a model that supports TOOL CALLING. Atlas needs the model to call the
   knowledge-base search tool. A model without tool support will ignore the library.
   Good choices to try first: Qwen3 4B (faster) or Qwen3 8B (smarter). DeepSeek R1 distills
   often handle tools poorly - test before you rely on one.
3. Make a project called "Atlas - Emergency":
     - Paste the text of Atlas_System_Prompt.txt as the project's system prompt.
     - Add every file in the Atlas_Cards folder to the project's knowledge base.
4. Optional second project "Atlas - Library": after the converter has run, copy a pack from
   ATLAS_for_OffGrid\\Packs\\ (for example 01_Medical.zip) to the phone, open the project's
   knowledge base and tap the package icon to import the whole pack at once.
   Start with 01_Medical and 06_Survival_Navigation - indexing on a phone is slow and too
   many books make searches worse. (Package icon = Off Grid Atlas app from coolchan03/Off-Grid.)
5. TEST it: ask "someone is bleeding badly from the leg, what do I do?" The answer should
   quote card E01. If it answers without searching, try a different model.

Copy the files to the phone with a USB cable (Phone > Download folder), then pick them
inside the app.
Backup: ATLAS_Pocket\\ATLAS_Pocket.html opens in any phone browser with no app at all.
"""

